From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Jul 2026 10:54:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07400/11362] [outer-loop] Checkpoint: preserve conductor's
 in-flight work before operator-requested stop

The autonomous conductor was stopped (systemctl --user stop) at the operator's
request, to prevent it fighting with upcoming manual work on the ARC candidate-
ranking/live-path code following tonight's REQ-ARC-FCP-5757 attribution finding.
It was mid-task at stop time; this commit preserves that partial work as a
checkpoint (same philosophy as the conductor's own checkpoint-commit fix from
earlier tonight, 174b31b28) rather than leaving it dangling or discarding it.
Not independently reviewed/validated -- preserved as-is per Never-Stash-Commit-
First discipline. ruff-format applied to clear the pre-commit format gate only;
no logic changes.

